ournal of Intercultural Studies"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/www.tandfonline.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1080\/07256860220122377","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2016,12,14]],"date-time":"2016-12-14T23:36:19Z","timestamp":1481758579000},"score":28.539577,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/www.tandfonline.com\/doi\/full\/10.1080\/07256860220122377"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2002,4]]},"references-count":29,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2010,8,3]]},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2002,4]]}},"alternative-id":["10.1080\/07256860220122377"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1080\/07256860220122377","ISSN":["0725-6868","1469-9540"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0725-6868","type":"print"},{"value":"1469-9540","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2002,4]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2024,3,10]],"date-time":"2024-03-10T12:10:11Z","timestamp":1710072611157},"reference-count":30,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2009,2,10]],"date-time":"2009-02-10T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1234224000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":4211,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Australian J of Anthropology"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1997,8]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Drawing upon life histories compiled in New Caledonia, this article examines the ways in which some women inscribed and contested their gendered subjectivities. Anchored in the perception that \u2018gender\u2019 can be recognised as historically and culturally constituted in contingent human practices, it proffers testimonies to reason that women's composition and expression of their lived experience can be understood as modes of embodied consciousness. By situating each woman's discursive strategy into the complex interplay of historical processes, structured social organisations, and the anomalies, ambiguities and contradictions revealed through their conversations, the relationships and practices which inscribed the self\u2010making of some Kanak and Caledonienne women are explored.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1111\/j.1835-9310.1997.tb00347.x","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2009,2,11]],"date-time":"2009-02-11T16:06:18Z","timestamp":1234368378000},"page":"145-166","update-policy":"http:\/\/dx.doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["The Right Kind of Women Things: Changing Compositions of Gendered Subjectivity in New Caledonia"],"prefix":"10.1111","volume":"8","author":[{"given":"Helen","family":"Johnson","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2010,3,8]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_1_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2307\/1354221"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_3_1","first-page":"45","volume-title":"Supposing the Subject","author":"Borch\u2010Jacobsen M.","year":"1994"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_4_1","volume-title":"Gender Trouble: Feminism and the Subversion of Identity","author":"Butler J.","year":"1990"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_5_1","first-page":"3","volume-title":"Feminists Theorize the Political","author":"Butler J.","year":"1992"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_6_1","volume-title":"Your Flag's Blocking Our Sun","author":"Chanter A.","year":"1990"},{"issue":"3","key":"e_1_2_1_7_1","first-page":"305","volume":"44","journal-title":"The Australian Journal of International Affairs"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2307\/j.ctvjf9x0h"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_9_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1525\/9780520946286-003"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_10_1","first-page":"65","volume-title":"Social Change in the Pacific Islands","author":"Connell J.","year":"1992"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_11_1","first-page":"vii","volume-title":"Supposing 